# Approval Gates

Ask before proceeding. Explain risk and propose a safe alternative when pausing.

## Always confirm

- Deleting or overwriting files
- Installing packages or dependencies
- Running database migrations
- Using credentials or touching secrets
- Committing or pushing to remote
- Deploying or publishing
- Sending large private context to remote models
- Expensive premium model runs on large tasks
- Changing production, medical, legal, financial, or hardware-critical outputs

## Default permission levels

| Level | Actions |
| --- | --- |
| Observe | Read, summarize — no edits |
| Plan | Inspect, propose plan — no edits |
| Edit | Modify files after plan acceptance |
| Execute | Run tests and safe local commands when approved |
| Integrate | Commit, PR — explicit approval only |
| External | Network deploys, production — explicit approval only |

Reference: `GOVERNANCE_AND_SAFETY.md`, `COFFEE_CONSTITUTION.md` Article 3.

## When pausing

State: what was requested, why it is risky, and the smallest safe next step (often Decaf Mode or a revised plan).
